# A Tour of Hyperactivity

Hyperactivity is a programming language, a proof assistant, and a decentralized operating system built on one primitive law: **local interaction**.

Most languages hand you a stack, a heap, a garbage collector, a separate type system, a separate build tool, and a separate network protocol. Hyperactivity replaces all of them with a single mathematical object: a **cubical interaction net**. Every program, every proof, every document, and even the web server serving this page is a net of cells wired together at ports, rewriting locally wherever an operation meets a value.

Every code example on this page is real Hyperactivity, typechecked by the machine itself (`build/cubical`). Wherever you see a **[Watch in Interaction Net Lab →](/nets)** link, you can watch and hear the exact cell rewrites happen live.

---

## 1. The One Law: Cells, Ports, and Active Pairs

Forget ASTs and evaluation stacks for a moment. In Hyperactivity, there is no primitive *thing* — only a primitive law of **interaction**:

- **Cell.** A node with one *principal port* (`●`) and zero or more *auxiliary ports*.
- **Value (`V_*`).** A cell that *offers* itself at its principal port: a function (`λ`), a pair `(a , b)`, a path (`λ i → t`), a constructor (`zero`, `suc`), a word (`#42`), a type.
- **Operation (`O_*`).** A cell that *consumes* one value at its principal port: application (`app`), projection (`fst`, `snd`), path application (`@ r`), substitution (`subst`), duplication (`dup`), erasure (`era`), Kan composition (`comp`), pattern matching (`case`).
- **Active pair.** An operation's principal port wired head-to-head (`●═══●`) to a value's principal port.

**This is the only place anything ever happens.** Two values wired together do nothing. Two operations wired together wait. When an operation meets a value, the two cells annihilate and are replaced by a tiny local net on their remaining wires. Nothing else in the universe is inspected.

```
  arg ──┐
        app ●═══● λ ── body     ⟶     out ── body  (with arg wired into the parameter)
  out ──┘
```

Because every rewrite touches only two cells and their immediate wires, disjoint active pairs never interfere. They fire in parallel on any number of workers with zero locks and identical results (confluence / causal invariance).

