## 5. Content-Addressed Source and Real-World Programs

Hyperactivity is not just a blackboard calculus — it is a complete systems language:

- **Words and Bytes.** Machine-native arbitrary-precision `Word`s (`#0`, `#42`, `wadd`, `weq`, `wshl`), raw `Bytes`, and zero-copy byte slices (`V_TEXT`).
- **Processes over the World (`Proc W A`).** Effects (files, sockets, syscalls, processes) are typed interaction trees (`Step W A`) executed by `#run`. The very HTTP server answering your browser right now (`lib/server.cub`) is a checked Hyperactivity program talking directly to the Linux kernel via `sys-call`.
- **Content-Addressed Pool (`store/`).** Code and documents are not mutable files overwritten in place. Every declaration is an immutable mathematical object identified by its SHA-256 content hash. A name is just a read-time overlay. Replacing a dependency `f` with `f'` constructs a new object beside the old one — and if `f ≡ f'`, every proof about callers transports automatically.

